{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"Cargo.toml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:46:35.581308Z","id":"a25be44a76101761b30631921da1fade2981b01b7a24499ac0e1fbdf27f07b92","body":{"detail":"cargo test, clippy and fmt in scripts/quality_gates.sh run on the root workspace only, so the VFS's tests (crates/clax-worker/vfs/tests) and the wasm32 build of clax-worker never run in a gate. The native tests also cover only the VFS against an in-memory PageStore: DoPageStore (crates/clax-worker/src/store.rs: the upsert/delete SQL, i64 and f64 bindings, transactionSync through Reflect) and the wasm SQLite build (sqlite-wasm-rs 0.5.5 with SQLITE_DEFAULT_CACHE_SIZE=-16384 and SQLITE_DEFAULT_PAGE_SIZE=8192, versus libsqlite3-sys natively) are exercised only by hand under wrangler dev.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":11},"end":{"line":12},"content_hash":"ff367854fd9e0067856a97495d8e9fdd046761208bd88ef5d9c19f95d00734c7"},"suggested_fix":"Add a lane running cargo test/clippy/fmt in crates/clax-worker, a wasm32 build check, and a scripted wrangler dev --local run of the routes (fill, abort, stats?check=1) across a restart.","summary":"No gate runs clax-worker or clax-do-vfs: the crates are outside the workspace and scripts/quality_gates.sh does not name them","tags":["gates","tests","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"Cargo.toml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:24:31.774226Z","id":"ef9746cdbe0a7102580a35291c8f4f7025c78312848d91f50afde3cb97b54dbf","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:0bf47593","summary":"Fixed in 0bf47593: lane_worker in scripts/quality_gates.sh runs, in crates/clax-worker, cargo fmt --check, cargo test --workspace, cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings, and node test-wasm.mjs, which runs build.sh, starts wrangler dev --local on free ports with a fresh --persist-to under crates/clax-worker/target/wasm-test/, writes through init, notes, abort, fill, journal and stats?check=1, restarts wrangler and compares notes, blobs, page counts, the blob digest and integrity_check. Evidence: each lane command, run alone on macOS, exits 0 (npm ci 17 s on its first run, fmt 0 s, test 5 s, clippy 1 s, test-wasm.mjs 15 s warm), and test-wasm.mjs ends with {\"ok\":true,...}. The Linux build in CI is unverified: see the concern on crates/clax-worker/build.sh:13:19.","supersedes":"a25be44a76101761b30631921da1fade2981b01b7a24499ac0e1fbdf27f07b92","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"CLA.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T03:59:18.868830Z","id":"af83eaac9e52ac2478b7435ddeced857822d39e56a98b7f41d0c827cb769de01","body":{"detail":"CLA.md (version 1.0) restates the terms of the Apache Software Foundation's Individual Contributor License Agreement for Empathic, Inc., with section 2 naming the right to distribute Contributions under GPL-2.0, AGPL-3.0 and any other terms Empathic chooses. It was drafted without legal review. Open: (1) review by counsel; (2) whether to add a commitment that Empathic will keep distributing Contributions under an OSI-approved license (some CLAs, such as the Harmony Agreements' outbound options, offer one; Apache's and Google's do not); (3) where signed copies are kept (CONTRIBUTING.md says email to alex@empathic.dev, kept by Empathic, unpublished).","kind":"concern","summary":"Have counsel review CLA.md before collecting signatures, and decide whether it promises an open-source outbound license","tags":["status:needs-decision","legal","session:claude-code:b2fe0abc-990b-4628-b4c7-4c6d7f3f261b"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"justfile","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:33:35.625613Z","id":"42e1d65c3e62b9776e3606fc30363c30d65d435394a2f0d5a06486dd42c7be7b","body":{"detail":"Failure: 'flutter test integration_test -d macos' with more than one *_test.dart file. The first file runs; each later one is built, then fails with 'Error waiting for a debug connection: The log reader stopped unexpectedly, or never started.' and 'Unable to start the app on the device'. Seen 2026-10-13 with locked_daemon_test.dart + full_loop_test.dart (target/flutter-app/i1.log) and with tool_loop_test.dart + full_loop_test.dart (target/flutter-app/i1-multi-v.log), with no other macOS build running. Each file passes in its own invocation (the built Debug app also starts on its own and prints its VM service URL). The cause inside flutter_tools or macOS was not found. apps/clax_app/integration_test/full_loop_test.dart now runs tool_loop.dart's test in its own launch, so the integration tests are two files: full_loop_test.dart and locked_daemon_test.dart.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":128},"end":{"line":129},"content_hash":"96540e8f8d84c7b159511b64ed2e76491a9fa247b2cc50b64c0fcc5e0a9d0fda"},"suggested_fix":"Run each file in its own invocation: 'cd apps/clax_app && for f in integration_test/*_test.dart; do flutter test \"$f\" -d macos || exit 1; done', or give the folder a single entry file that calls each scenario.","summary":"just app-integration launches one app per test file, and on macOS every file after the first fails to launch","tags":["integration","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"MODULE.bazel","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T19:00:08.328869Z","id":"74b6aeeeaf76b82f813f86b7f67ee1da9f61b9e3acc4bbbe08b46739b14eb4b9","body":{"detail":"rules_flutter (github.com/aran/rules_flutter, 0.0.6, released 2026-10-16) was taken: it fetches Flutter 3.47.7, its engines and every pub package by checksum, compiles kernel and AOT, runs flutter_tester, and builds APKs with rules_android and macOS apps with rules_apple, on Bazel 9. It is alpha (its README: 'the public API may still change'), one maintainer, and needed three patches here (bazel/flutter/rules_flutter.patch) and a composed APK macro (bazel/flutter/android.bzl). Writing the same from scratch was not worth it while it is maintained.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":161},"end":{"line":185},"content_hash":"3e9da6d4ded7f6f517d7abc6d543921a147131562f57756d9e38b5259b5e40e8"},"summary":"Own Starlark rules for Flutter instead of rules_flutter","tags":["revisit:rules_flutter goes a quarter without a release, or a version bump breaks bazel/flutter/","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"justfile","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T19:00:08.329361Z","id":"c6d27cf4629f0a837c06af20b2dffd2efd222962a089e00a182e007424e5083e","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"42e1d65c3e62b9776e3606fc30363c30d65d435394a2f0d5a06486dd42c7be7b","summary":"With Bazel, just app-integration runs each file as its own app and test target (//apps/clax_app:integration_<name>, exclusive), not one flutter test call: on 2026-10-17 integration_locked_daemon and integration_bundle passed in one bazelisk test invocation with integration_full_loop (which failed in its second test, as it does under flutter test too). The native recipe (just app-integration-native) still runs one flutter test per file.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"Cargo.lock","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T05:02:17.087090Z","id":"c12c3723612ad0bff82154a551ce6cb82b995cdf95ac50be754e4ee3f165cdc2","body":{"detail":"Apache-2.0-only code is incompatible with GPL-2.0-only (LICENSE lists apps/clax_app under GPL-2.0-only). rmcp is the MCP SDK used by crates/clax-commands and crates/clax-mcp (Cargo.toml: rmcp.workspace); rmcp-macros (Cargo.lock:2185) is its proc-macro. bazel cquery 'deps(//crates/clax-cli:clax_android_arm64)' reaches both, so the APK's libclax.so carries rmcp. The same crates are in main's GPL-2.0-only clax (relicensed in 316f985e2 without a recorded audit of third-party crates), so the decision is the whole project's. Options: (a) an additional permission in LICENSE for Apache-2.0 libraries; (b) replace rmcp with an MCP implementation under a GPL-2.0-compatible license (MIT or BSD), or Clax's own.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2151},"end":{"line":2160},"content_hash":"1109079ada30e5ed1b5f71aeb0e97e4f40a4286f8125862d0c244d083b7f5154"},"summary":"The app's clax (and main's GPL-2.0-only clax) links rmcp 3.5.0 and rmcp-macros, Apache-2.0 only","tags":["license","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"Cargo.lock","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T05:02:17.087182Z","id":"9200d22d888cc4b91885724ab2409c01cedbebd8d89518dcc3d40020c5e18cb1","body":{"detail":"Apache-2.0-only code is incompatible with GPL-2.0-only (LICENSE lists apps/clax_app under GPL-2.0-only). ring is a direct dependency of crates/clax-core (Cargo.toml: ring.workspace) and of rustls, which reqwest uses for TLS; its Cargo.toml declares 'Apache-2.0 AND ISC', so its Apache-2.0 parts bind. It is in the APK's libclax.so and in main's GPL-2.0-only clax alike. Options: (a) an additional permission in LICENSE for Apache-2.0 libraries; (b) move clax-core's use to RustCrypto crates (MIT OR Apache-2.0) and rustls to a RustCrypto provider; aws-lc-rs is no better (Apache-2.0 AND ISC, OpenSSL).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2137},"end":{"line":2142},"content_hash":"743516077ba59fac4071bdab0ed4e015cc351a70125edde9183104e8efbc12ab"},"summary":"The app's clax (and main's) links ring 0.17.14, licensed Apache-2.0 AND ISC, under GPL-2.0-only","tags":["license","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"Cargo.lock","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T05:02:17.087268Z","id":"2e6e83c78b053e2730e47956d1d6b3039c9b7b1d2c48591dc8ada2550b09e681","body":{"detail":"Apache-2.0-only code is incompatible with GPL-2.0-only (LICENSE lists apps/clax_app under GPL-2.0-only). sync_wrapper is a dependency of axum, axum-core, tower and reqwest (Cargo.lock), not of Clax's own code, and is in the APK's libclax.so and main's GPL-2.0-only clax alike. Options: (a) an additional permission in LICENSE for Apache-2.0 libraries (practical: axum, tower and reqwest all need it); (b) ask upstream to dual-license it MIT OR Apache-2.0, as most of the ecosystem is.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2635},"end":{"line":2640},"content_hash":"0cdb210e1d4931cbcc8570105a759bb82f731749807f367f3fcc855047791479"},"summary":"The app's clax (and main's) links sync_wrapper 1.0.2, Apache-2.0 only, through axum, tower and reqwest","tags":["license","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"MODULE.bazel","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T09:39:08.877840Z","id":"aa6f6613eac5a56b2e2a97cf0a6ec009de378ab7011e438c0c9bd2d2022d6e4f","body":{"detail":"@androidsdk unpacks every row of its archives whenever it is fetched (every APK build), and bazel/android/rules_android.patch fails for a directory with no row for the host OS, so the rows would also need a Linux emulator. The system image unpacks to 4.4 GB. As @android_emulator and @android_system_image only //apps/clax_app:integration_android_* (and scripts/app-android-emulator.sh) fetch them.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":288},"end":{"line":313},"content_hash":"a717eb3cb9959674168ff0efdf1b26aa92eda0f045d3d780c157ad5b5f16cc61"},"summary":"The Android emulator and system image are http_archives of their own, not rows of android_sdk.configure's archives","tags":["revisit:a target other than the manual Android integration tests needs the emulator or the system image","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"Cargo.lock","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T22:27:54.171109Z","id":"d2fea0b88b294c35d4c7bac7b73786689050782efc54523866f0eeed022e3897","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"c12c3723612ad0bff82154a551ce6cb82b995cdf95ac50be754e4ee3f165cdc2","summary":"The app no longer ships //crates/clax-cli:clax_android_*: it ships the embedded core, and clax-embed still reaches rmcp and rmcp-macros through clax-server and clax-mcp (cargo metadata --offline: clax-embed's normal dependency closure includes rmcp and rmcp-macros), so this stands for the APK's, the Mac app's and the iOS app's core.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
